@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title GitHub credentials — why the config mount alone is not enough

' covers: cmd/proveo/ghtoken.go

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN\nexplicit env" as ENV <<app>>
  component """gh auth token --hostname github.com""\nbounded 5s" as GH <<app>>
  database "macOS login KEYCHAIN\nthe default `gh auth login` store" as KC <<db>>
  database "~/.config/gh/hosts.yml\ntoken only when gh put one there" as HOSTS <<db>>
  component "prompt — run ""gh auth login""?" as PROMPT <<app>>
}

node "Container" as CONT <<host>> {
  component "-e GH_TOKEN  (BARE name)" as FWD <<app>>
  component "ubi recipes\n5000/hr authenticated" as UBI <<app>>
}

component "token on the docker argv\nvisible in ""ps""" as LEAK <<error>>
component "anonymous 60/hr per SOURCE IP\nsilent loss of code intelligence" as ANON <<error>>

ENV ARROW_MAIN FWD : first match wins
GH ARROW_MAIN FWD
KC ARROW_MAIN GH : reachable ONLY from the host
HOSTS ARROW_OPTIONAL GH : often holds no token
GH ARROW_OPTIONAL PROMPT : nothing stored
PROMPT ARROW_MAIN KC : gh stores it; proveo keeps no copy
FWD ARROW_MAIN UBI
FWD ARROW_ERROR LEAK : what the bare name AVOIDS
UBI ARROW_ERROR ANON : when no token is reachable

note bottom of HOSTS
  **The false premise.** ""ghConfigMount"" binds ~/.config/gh read-only so ""gh""
  inside the container reuses the operator's session, and its rationale assumed
  hosts.yml holds the OAuth token. That is true only when gh stored one there —
  ""--with-token"", CI, or a host with no system keyring.

  The default macOS flow puts the token in the login keychain and leaves
  hosts.yml with a username and nothing else. The mount then lands a config with
  no credential: ""gh auth token"" inside the container returns empty, and the
  entrypoint's own check has always reported "gh session not authenticated".
end note

note right of GH
  Bounded at 5s, mirroring the cap the entrypoint puts on ""gh auth status"". A
  warm keychain answers in ~30ms, but a LOCKED one blocks behind a GUI
  authorization prompt a CLI run can never satisfy — and a timeout is reported
  as its own case, because telling an operator who IS logged in to run
  ""gh auth login"" sends them down the wrong path.

  ""--hostname github.com"" is pinned because ubi resolves against api.github.com:
  an operator authenticated only to a GitHub Enterprise host must fall through
  to unauthenticated rather than forward a token that host will reject.
end note

note right of FWD
  Forwarded by BARE name so the value comes from proveo's own environment rather
  than the docker argv — the same mechanism the missing-env wizard uses to keep
  provider secrets out of ""ps"". Reading the token grants the installer nothing
  the agent could not already obtain by running ""gh auth token"" itself; passing
  it to one command rather than exporting it keeps it out of the agent's
  environment.
end note

note bottom of PROMPT
  Interactive only (TTY + ""run.WizardEnabled""). A headless run — CI, the E2E suite,
  a cron agent — warns and continues, because the cost of no token is rate limit,
  never correctness. Storage is gh's own: after a successful login every later
  run resolves silently, and proveo persists no credential of its own.
end note
@enduml
